  </div>

  <h2>Plan without exposing real future commitments</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to reveal a real employer, client, appointment, address, trip, ticket, booking, schedule, contract, payment, password, family commitment, health visit, study plan, or private future intention. Use Mika, Ravi, the Harborline fair, and the fictional event board. Real details are optional.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>New problems:</b> Respond to two setup problems with one immediate decision and one offer using <span class="ex">will</span>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Prior plan and evidence:</b> Report one earlier intention and one present trajectory with <span class="ex">be going to</span>. State the supporting decision or evidence.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Arrangements and schedules:</b> Give two organized arrangements with practical details and two official schedule times.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Dependencies:</b> Use <span class="ex">when, as soon as, until</span>, or <span class="ex">if</span> to connect a later result to a future time or condition.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: give a 75–90 second fictional event briefing</h3>
    <p>Use a supplied Harborline event board with two new problems, two earlier decisions, two visible warning signs, three confirmed appointments, and two official schedule entries. Give an immediate response, offer, promise, neutral forecast, prior intention, present-trajectory forecast, arrangement, and schedule. Connect at least two later actions with future time or condition clauses. For one event, state two grammatical forms and explain the different viewpoint each would foreground.</p>
    <p><b>Evidence check:</b> Can the listener identify when each decision existed, what present evidence supports a forecast, which practical detail organizes an arrangement, which authority owns a schedule, where each future clause begins, and why an alternative form may also be grammatical?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You distinguished an immediate response, prior intention, present trajectory, organized arrangement, official schedule, and future-time clause from their complete contexts.">
