  <h2>Reflect: what does the speaker foreground now?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the decision path</h3>
    <p>Complete these ideas aloud: <span class="ex">I use will when I present...</span> <span class="ex">I use going to when I foreground...</span> <span class="ex">I use the Present Continuous when...</span> <span class="ex">I use the Present Simple for a schedule when...</span> <span class="ex">After future-time when or as soon as, I...</span> <span class="ex">Two forms can both be grammatical when...</span></p>
    <p>Take one fictional fair event and report it as a prior intention, then as a confirmed arrangement. Explain what new practical detail licenses the shift. Take one forecast and report it neutrally with <span class="ex">will</span>, then foreground a present trajectory with <span class="ex">going to</span>.</p>
